      "id": "subtract-negative-numbers",
      "title": "Turn subtraction into addition",
      "explanation": "Each parenthesized number is negative, so subtracting it adds its positive opposite. The expression becomes\n\\[\n1+2-3+4-5+6.\n\\]\nGrouping nearby terms gives\n\\[\n(1+2)+(-3+4)+(-5+6)=3+1+1=\\boxed{5}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
